*---------------------------------------------------------------
* mm.procbank.equ -- process-bank entry constants: the load
* address and the argv header/pointer-array addresses every
* spawned program's own liba startup code reads. Split out of
* inc/memmap.equ (docs/SELFHOST-CONVERSION.md phase 1) as
* its OWN file, smaller than the rest of docs/MEMMAP.md #3,
* because these three symbols are the only ones nearly every
* compilation unit needs -- every src/bin/*.s program PUTs this
* file (via inc/startup.equ's ARGC/ARGV derivation) whether
* or not it ever touches argv, spawn, or the $BF00 overlay.
* inc/mm.procbnk2.equ holds the rest of docs/MEMMAP.md
* #3 (heap top, overlay, LC storage, the $FFxx page) and PUTs
* AFTER this file wherever both are needed, since its own
* derivations (SB_WINDOW, ARG_MAX) reference LOAD_BASE below.
* Full design notes: I.MEMMAPE.TXT (docs/a2/), docs/MEMMAP.md #3
*---------------------------------------------------------------

* See I.MEMMAPE.TXT: "3. Canonical process-bank layout (docs/ME"

LOAD_BASE       equ   $0800       ;exec entry point / process
                                  ;image load addr

* -- The argv block a spawn() stages into the child, inside
* -- PRC_LOWFREE (docs/MEMMAP.md #3.2, docs/SYSCALL.md ruling
* -- 13, inc/startup.equ's ARGC/ARGV). Named HERE, once:
* -- src/kernel/process.s used to declare its own copies of
* -- these three addresses while startup.equ derived ARGC/ARGV
* -- from PRC_LOWFREE separately, which is how two layers came
* -- to disagree about the same layout (docs/LIMITS.md).
* -- THE ENVIRONMENT SHARES THE BLOCK (docs/SYSCALL.md item 13c,
* -- 2026-08-22), Unix-style: envc and envp's pointer array
* -- follow argv's inside PRC_ARGV_PTRS, and envp's strings
* -- follow argv's inside PRC_ARGV_STR. Only argc's own address
* -- is fixed; envc sits at PRC_ARGV_PTRS+2*argc, which is why
* -- src/liba/env.s computes it at runtime instead of naming it
* -- here.
PRC_ARGV_HDR   equ   $0200       ;argc, 1 byte (== PRC_LOWFREE)
PRC_ARGV_PTRS  equ   $0201       ;pointer arrays: argc*2 bytes,
                                  ;then envc, then envc*2 bytes

* -- PRC_LC_TOP: the first byte a process's language card does
* -- NOT own -- the kernel's $FFxx syscall door. An LC-resident
* -- table ends with `err */PRC_LC_TOP` (ex.s, vi.s, nulib2.s).
PRC_LC_TOP  equ   $FF00
